       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg per day, which is twice the usual maximum for adults. The maximum is 3,200 mg/day, and that's only for specific inpatient or prescriber-directed use. A dose this high carries a serious risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nCommon ibuprofen regimens for adults include:\n- **400 mg orally every 6 hours (four times daily)**, which is 1,600 mg/day.\n- **600 mg orally four times daily**, which is 2,400 mg/day.\n- **800 mg orally three times daily**, which is 2,400 mg/day.\n- **800 mg orally four times daily**, which is 3,200 mg/day. This is the ceiling and is usually reserved for specific indications.\n\nThe order may have meant 1,600 mg total per day, or 400 mg or 800 mg per dose. Please confirm the intended dose. Because this order is outside normal limits, the treating clinician or prescriber should also confirm and place it, or approve it. Once I have a confirmed dose, I can enter it right away."
