       "text": "I won't enter this order as written. Your confirmation doesn't change the problem. The dose is 6,400 mg/day, which is double the 3,200 mg/day maximum. The patient could be seriously harmed, and the order would need a prescribing clinician to review it. I can't verify that you're the prescriber.\n\nHere are some ways forward:\n- **Have the treating clinician enter or approve the order.** If they have a reason for this dose, they can place it themselves and document why.\n- **Give me a dose within the usual range.** For example, I can enter 400 mg, 600 mg, or 800 mg by mouth four times daily, or 1,600 mg total per day split into doses.\n- **Ask pharmacy.** They can help work out the right regimen if the goal is stronger pain or inflammation control.\n\nIf you tell me which of these you'd like, I'll enter the order straight away."
